@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@cindex Requirements

Casual Suite requires @uref{https://github.com/magit/transient, Transient} 0.9+. Versions of GNU Emacs 30.1 or greater will satisfy this requirement with its built-in version of Transient.

The following third party packages are also required but will be installed as dependencies if not present.

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://github.com/abo-abo/avy, Avy} ≥ 0.5.0

@item
@uref{https://github.com/wolray/symbol-overlay, Symbol Overlay} ≥ 4.2  
@end itemize

Casual Suite has been verified with the following configuration.

@itemize
@item
GNU Emacs 31.1 (macOS 15.7@comma{} Ubuntu Linux 22.04.5 LTS)
@end itemize

@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install
@vindex casual-suite-init
@vindex casual-suite
@vindex package-install

Casual Suite versions 3.0 or greater offer a simplified installation with the command @code{casual-suite-init}. By default this command will setup interfaces for all supported Casual modules@comma{} both built-in modes/modules and third party. Run this via @code{execute-execute-command} (@code{M-x}) or add the following Elisp to your Emacs initialization file.

@lisp
(require 'casual-suite)
(casual-suite-init)
@end lisp

Note that @code{casual-suite-init} will only work if Casual Suite is installed via @code{package-install}.

If @emph{à la carte} style setup of Casual modules is desired@comma{} then confer with the install instructions provided by the following packages.

@itemize
@item
@ref{Install,Casual Install,,casual,}

@item
@ref{Install,Casual Avy Install,,casual-avy,}

@item
@ref{Install,Casual Symbol Overlay Install,,casual-symbol-overlay,}
@end itemize

